    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">beverage</span> is any drink, other than plain water, consumed to quench thirst, provide refreshment, nourishment or stimulation. Beverages are broadly classified into alcoholic and non-alcoholic types.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Beverages</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Beverages are liquids prepared and consumed for drinking, ranging from simple fruit juices to complex fermented drinks, and they play an important social, cultural and nutritional role.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Classification of Beverages</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Alcoholic beverages</td><td>Drinks containing ethanol produced through fermentation (and sometimes distillation)</td><td>Beer, wine, spirits (gin, whisky), palm wine, burukutu</td></tr><tr><td>Non-alcoholic beverages</td><td>Drinks that contain no (or negligible) alcohol</td><td>Tea, coffee, cocoa, fruit juices, soft drinks, milk drinks</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Nutritive Value of Beverages</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li><strong>Milk-based beverages</strong> (cocoa, milk drinks) supply protein, calcium and some vitamins.</li><li><strong>Fruit juices</strong> supply vitamin C and other vitamins, minerals and natural sugars.</li><li><strong>Tea and coffee</strong> contain stimulants (tannin, caffeine) but little nutritive value, apart from any milk or sugar added.</li><li><strong>Alcoholic beverages</strong> supply energy (calories) from alcohol and carbohydrate content but lack significant protein, vitamins or minerals, and excessive intake can harm health.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Characteristics of Alcoholic Beverages</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Produced through fermentation of sugars by yeast, sometimes followed by distillation.</li><li>Contain ethanol, which has intoxicating and energy-providing properties.</li><li>Often have a distinctive taste, aroma and colour depending on the source material.</li><li>Consumption is regulated by age and, in some cultures, religious restrictions.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Characteristics of Non-Alcoholic Beverages</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Contain no or negligible alcohol content.</li><li>Suitable for all age groups, including children.</li><li>Can be nutritious (milk-based, fruit juices) or largely stimulant-based (tea, coffee).</li><li>Widely used for refreshment, hospitality and social occasions.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to classify a list of given drinks into alcoholic and non-alcoholic categories, and to state at least one nutrient or component found in each.</div>",
