    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Practical competence in preparing beverages and special diet dishes is an essential WASSCE skill, requiring correct technique, hygiene and presentation.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Preparing and Serving Beverages</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Beverage</th><th>Key preparation points</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cocoa</td><td>Blend cocoa powder with a little cold milk/water to a paste before adding hot milk, to avoid lumps</td></tr><tr><td>Coffee</td><td>Use freshly boiled water; avoid prolonged boiling, which destroys flavour and aroma</td></tr><tr><td>Tea</td><td>Warm the teapot first; use freshly boiled water poured directly onto tea leaves/bags; infuse briefly</td></tr><tr><td>Fruit drinks/juice</td><td>Extract juice hygienically; serve chilled, close to preparation time to preserve vitamin C</td></tr><tr><td>Egg flip</td><td>Whisk egg with milk and sugar/flavouring; serve immediately, often lightly warmed, not boiled</td></tr><tr><td>Milk drinks</td><td>Warm milk gently; avoid prolonged boiling to preserve nutrients and prevent curdling</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Preparing and Serving Special Diet Dishes</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li><strong>Vegetarian dishes:</strong> use plant proteins (beans, soybeans, groundnuts, lentils) to ensure adequate protein intake.</li><li><strong>Weight-reduction dishes:</strong> use low-fat cooking methods (grilling, steaming, boiling) and high-fibre ingredients.</li><li><strong>Diabetic dishes:</strong> control portion size and use complex carbohydrates with a low glycaemic index; avoid added sugar.</li><li><strong>Ulcer-friendly dishes:</strong> prepare mild, non-spicy meals, avoiding excessive pepper, citrus and fried foods.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. General Practical Guidelines</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Maintain strict personal and kitchen hygiene throughout preparation.</li><li>Measure ingredients accurately for consistent, appropriate nutrient content.</li><li>Garnish and present dishes attractively and appropriately for the intended consumer.</li><li>Taste (where appropriate) and adjust seasoning carefully, especially for restricted diets.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> In practicals, examiners assess hygiene, correct technique, and suitability of the dish for its stated special diet — not just taste and appearance.</div>",
