    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Traditional dishes</span> are foods prepared according to the customs and recipes passed down within a particular locality or ethnic group, while <span class=\"learn-keyword\">foreign dishes</span> originate from other countries or cultures.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Traditional and Foreign Dishes</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Traditional dishes reflect the ingredients, cooking methods and tastes native to a specific community, often prepared for everyday meals or special occasions. Foreign dishes are those adopted or adapted from cuisines outside one's own culture, often through trade, migration or globalisation.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Examples of Nigerian Traditional Dishes by Locality</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Locality/Ethnic group</th><th>Example traditional dishes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Yoruba</td><td>Amala and ewedu, moin-moin, ewa agoyin</td></tr><tr><td>Igbo</td><td>Ofe nsala (white soup), abacha (African salad), ugba</td></tr><tr><td>Hausa</td><td>Tuwo shinkafa, miyan kuka, fura da nono</td></tr><tr><td>Niger Delta/South-South</td><td>Banga soup, starch and fisherman soup, afang soup</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Examples of Foreign Dishes by Origin</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Origin</th><th>Example dishes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>European</td><td>Roast beef, spaghetti bolognese, fish and chips</td></tr><tr><td>American</td><td>Hamburger, hot dog, apple pie</td></tr><tr><td>Japanese</td><td>Sushi, ramen, tempura</td></tr><tr><td>Chinese</td><td>Fried rice (Chinese-style), spring rolls, chow mein</td></tr><tr><td>Indian</td><td>Curry, biryani, samosa</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Significance of Traditional and Foreign Dishes</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Traditional dishes preserve cultural identity and are often tied to significant occasions and ceremonies.</li><li>Foreign dishes broaden culinary knowledge and diversify diet, especially in urban and cosmopolitan settings.</li><li>Both contribute to tourism, as food is a major aspect of cultural exchange.</li><li>Fusion cooking increasingly blends traditional and foreign techniques and ingredients.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to name at least one traditional dish from a specified Nigerian ethnic group and one foreign dish from a specified country.</div>",
