    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Practical skill in preparing both traditional ethnic dishes and selected foreign dishes demonstrates versatility and cultural food knowledge expected at the WASSCE level.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Preparing Traditional Dishes</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Source authentic, fresh local ingredients wherever possible.</li><li>Follow the traditional preparation sequence and cooking method associated with the dish (e.g. correct pounding, grinding, or fermentation steps).</li><li>Pay attention to the characteristic texture, consistency and seasoning typical of the dish.</li><li>Present the dish in a manner consistent with local tradition (e.g. appropriate accompaniment, serving vessel).</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Preparing Foreign Dishes</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Follow the specific recipe and method associated with the dish's country of origin.</li><li>Source appropriate ingredients or identify suitable local substitutes where original ingredients are unavailable.</li><li>Apply the correct foreign cooking technique (e.g. stir-frying for Chinese dishes, baking for many European and American dishes).</li><li>Garnish and present the dish in keeping with its foreign culinary tradition.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Common Assessment Criteria</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>What is assessed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Authenticity</td><td>Whether the dish reflects the correct traditional or foreign style</td></tr><tr><td>Technique</td><td>Correct use of appropriate preparation and cooking methods</td></tr><tr><td>Hygiene</td><td>Cleanliness throughout preparation and serving</td></tr><tr><td>Presentation</td><td>Appropriate garnishing, plating and serving style</td></tr><tr><td>Taste and texture</td><td>Appropriate seasoning, doneness and consistency for the dish type</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the typical accompaniment for common Nigerian soups and swallows (e.g. amala with ewedu, tuwo with miyan kuka), as this is often tested alongside preparation steps.</div>",
