    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Entrepreneurship</span> in catering involves identifying an opportunity in the food business and organising the resources needed to establish and run a successful catering enterprise.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Key Definitions</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Entrepreneur</td><td>A person who identifies a business opportunity and takes the risk of organising resources to start and run a business</td></tr><tr><td>Entrepreneurship</td><td>The process of planning, organising and managing a business venture, along with its risks, to make a profit</td></tr><tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>A business organisation or venture, especially one involving initiative and risk-taking</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Characteristics of Entrepreneurship</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Innovation and creativity in identifying and meeting a need.</li><li>Willingness to take calculated risks.</li><li>Self-motivation, discipline and perseverance.</li><li>Good planning and organisational ability.</li><li>Ability to manage resources (money, time, people, ingredients) efficiently.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Advantages and Disadvantages of Entrepreneurship</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Advantages</th><th>Disadvantages</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Independence and control over one's work</td><td>Financial risk, including possible loss of investment</td></tr><tr><td>Potential for significant profit</td><td>Irregular or unpredictable income, especially at the start</td></tr><tr><td>Flexibility in scheduling and decision-making</td><td>Long working hours, especially in early stages</td></tr><tr><td>Opportunity to create jobs for others</td><td>High levels of responsibility and stress</td></tr><tr><td>Personal fulfilment from building something of one's own</td><td>Need for broad skills (cooking, marketing, finance, management)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Factors Contributing to the Success of an Enterprise</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>A clear understanding of the target market and customer needs.</li><li>Consistent quality and hygiene standards.</li><li>Sound financial planning and record-keeping.</li><li>Effective marketing and good customer relations.</li><li>Reliable sourcing of ingredients and supplies.</li><li>Adaptability to changing trends and customer feedback.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Setting Up a Catering Enterprise</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Identify a specific catering niche (e.g. small chops, event catering, confectionery, packed lunches).</li><li>Conduct market research to understand demand, competitors and pricing.</li><li>Draw up a simple business plan, including costs and expected income.</li><li>Secure appropriate equipment, workspace and ingredient suppliers.</li><li>Register the business and comply with relevant food safety regulations.</li><li>Develop a marketing strategy (word of mouth, social media, sampling).</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to list at least three characteristics of a successful entrepreneur AND three factors that make a catering business succeed — these are commonly tested separately.</div>",
