    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Carrying out practical cookery exercises allows students to apply their knowledge of recipes, interpretation and scheduling to produce an actual finished dish under realistic conditions.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. From Plan to Practice</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Having interpreted a cookery assignment and prepared a detailed schedule, students carry out the actual cooking exercise, applying recipe knowledge, correct techniques and good hygiene practice throughout.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Key Practical Skills Demonstrated</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Accurate measuring and weighing of ingredients.</li><li>Correct use of cooking methods appropriate to the dish (boiling, frying, baking, steaming, grilling, etc.).</li><li>Good time management, following the prepared schedule closely.</li><li>Maintaining hygiene and safety standards throughout preparation.</li><li>Adapting smoothly if minor issues arise during cooking.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Applying Recipe Knowledge</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Following ingredient quantities and preparation steps accurately.</li><li>Adjusting seasoning and consistency appropriately as the dish develops.</li><li>Recognising signs of doneness (colour, texture, aroma) without relying solely on the clock.</li><li>Ensuring the final dish matches the intended outcome described in the recipe.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Common Challenges During Practical Exercises</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Running behind schedule due to underestimated preparation time.</li><li>Equipment or ingredient shortages requiring quick adaptation.</li><li>Maintaining composure and hygiene under the pressure of time constraints.</li><li>Balancing multiple dishes cooking simultaneously.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Reflection After Practice</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">After completing a practical exercise, it is valuable to reflect on what went well, what could be improved, and whether the schedule and recipe needs adjustment for next time — this reflective habit builds steady improvement in practical competence.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Examiners look for evidence that the finished dish matches the stated requirements of the original question — always double-check your dish against the original brief before presenting it.</div>",
