    "topic": "Practical Assessment",
    "topicCode": "SS3-FN-17",
    "module": "Practical Skills and Assessment",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The practical assessment brings together all the skills developed through the term — interpretation, scheduling, cooking and presentation — in a single, formally evaluated exercise.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Components of a Practical Assessment</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>What is assessed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interpretation and planning</td><td>Whether the candidate correctly understood the brief and planned an appropriate response</td></tr><tr><td>Food preparation skills</td><td>Correct technique, hygiene, and use of appropriate cooking methods</td></tr><tr><td>Finished dish quality</td><td>Taste, texture, doneness and overall success of the final product</td></tr><tr><td>Presentation</td><td>Garnishing, plating and visual appeal of the finished dish</td></tr><tr><td>Table setting and service</td><td>Correct application of table setting and service techniques where required</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Demonstrating Practical Skills</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Show clear evidence of planning (written interpretation and schedule) before cooking begins.</li><li>Work efficiently and hygienically throughout the session.</li><li>Manage time to complete the dish within the stipulated period.</li><li>Use correct techniques for the specific cooking methods required.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Presenting Finished Food Items</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Choose appropriate serving dishes and utensils for the food type.</li><li>Garnish thoughtfully, using edible, relevant garnishes that complement the dish.</li><li>Ensure correct serving temperature (hot foods served hot, cold foods served cold).</li><li>Arrange food neatly and proportionately on the serving dish.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Applying Table Setting and Service in Practice</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Set the table appropriately for the type of meal being presented (formal or informal).</li><li>Arrange cutlery, crockery and glassware in the correct order and position.</li><li>Demonstrate correct serving technique if required as part of the assessment.</li><li>Maintain overall neatness and attention to detail in the complete presentation.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Preparing for a Successful Practical Assessment</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Practise the chosen or likely dishes multiple times before the actual assessment.</li><li>Review and refine time schedules based on previous practice sessions.</li><li>Ensure familiarity with all equipment that will be used.</li><li>Revise key theory (food classes, special diets, hygiene rules) that may support practical decisions.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Practical assessment marks are awarded across the WHOLE process — planning, technique, hygiene, and presentation — not just for how the finished dish tastes.</div>",
